#: ../../../ExternalClangExamples.md:1
msgid "External Clang Examples"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ExternalClangExamples.md:3
msgid "Introduction"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ExternalClangExamples.md:5
msgid ""
"This page provides some examples of the kinds of things that people have "
"done with Clang that might serve as useful guides (or starting points) from "
"which to develop your own tools. They may be helpful even for something as "
"banal (but necessary) as how to set up your build to integrate Clang."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ExternalClangExamples.md:10
msgid ""
"Clang's library-based design is deliberately aimed at facilitating use by "
"external projects, and we are always interested in improving Clang to better "
"serve our external users. Some typical categories of applications where "
"Clang is used are:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ExternalClangExamples.md:15
msgid "Static analysis."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ExternalClangExamples.md:16
msgid "Documentation/cross-reference generation."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ExternalClangExamples.md:18
msgid ""
"If you know of (or wrote!) a tool or project using Clang, please post on "
"[the Discourse forums (Clang Frontend category)](https://discourse.llvm.org/"
"c/clang/6) to have it added. (or if you are already a Clang contributor, "
"feel free to directly commit additions). Since the primary purpose of this "
"page is to provide examples that can help developers, generally they must "
"have code available."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ExternalClangExamples.md:24
msgid "List of projects and tools"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ExternalClangExamples.md:26
msgid ""
"[https://github.com/Andersbakken/rtags/](https://github.com/Andersbakken/"
"rtags/)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ExternalClangExamples.md:28
msgid ""
"\"RTags is a client/server application that indexes c/c++ code and keeps a "
"persistent in-memory database of references, symbolnames, completions etc.\""
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ExternalClangExamples.md:32
msgid ""
"[https://rprichard.github.io/CxxCodeBrowser/](https://rprichard.github.io/"
"CxxCodeBrowser/)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ExternalClangExamples.md:34
msgid "\"A C/C++ source code indexer and navigator.\""
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ExternalClangExamples.md:36
msgid ""
"[https://github.com/etaoins/qconnectlint](https://github.com/etaoins/"
"qconnectlint)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ExternalClangExamples.md:38
msgid ""
"\"qconnectlint is a Clang tool for statically verifying the consistency of "
"signal and slot connections made with Qt's `QObject::connect`.\""
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ExternalClangExamples.md:41
msgid ""
"[https://github.com/woboq/woboq_codebrowser](https://github.com/woboq/"
"woboq_codebrowser)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ExternalClangExamples.md:43
msgid ""
"\"The Woboq Code Browser is a web-based code browser for C/C++ projects. "
"Check out [https://code.woboq.org/](https://code.woboq.org/) for an example!"
"\""
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ExternalClangExamples.md:46
msgid "[https://github.com/mozilla/dxr](https://github.com/mozilla/dxr)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ExternalClangExamples.md:48
msgid ""
"\"DXR is a source code cross-reference tool that uses static analysis data "
"collected by instrumented compilers.\""
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ExternalClangExamples.md:51
msgid ""
"[https://github.com/eschulte/clang-mutate](https://github.com/eschulte/clang-"
